<section class="shell band">
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Supervision here is clinical work rather than paperwork, and the lens is the same
    whether you are a supervisee or a client: IFS-informed EMDR for processing, Somatic
    Experiencing for pace, NARM for the pattern underneath. If you want to understand what is
    happening in the room and not only sign off hours, this is that practice. Reem Glasco,
    LPC-S, has held Texas supervisor status since 2009 and is an EMDRIA Approved Consultant, a
    NARM therapist and a Somatic Experiencing Practitioner, in Austin, Texas. Supervision runs
    $425 a month online statewide and EMDR consultation $185 an hour, and some of the work
    happens on a trail or with horses rather than on a screen. Clients seeking therapy are seen
    by Reem or by the practice's associates.</p>
  </div>
</section>



